# Deny list for bin/privacy-scan.sh. Copy to config/privacy-deny.local, which
# is gitignored, and list the literal names that must never reach this public
# repository: the company, the product, the deployment directory, the hosts.
#
# One POSIX extended regular expression per line, matched case-insensitively
# against both added diff lines and, with --tree, every tracked line. Blank
# lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored. An absent file is not an
# error, so the gate still runs with its generic patterns alone.
#
# No pattern can guess an organisation's name, which is why this file exists
# and why it stays out of the tree: writing the name into a public file to
# keep the name out of public files is the same leak by another route.
#
# Examples, with invented names:
# acmecorp
# acme-payroll
# (ap|dev|preprod)\.acme\.example
